Objective

I have an existing Underwriting AI solution codebase containing multiple AI agents. The existing solution works, but it was designed without a persona/Role AI Agent layer.

I have now been provided an Excel workbook that defines a new target architecture based on personas (Role AI Agents). The workbook contains sheets describing:

* Role AI Agents / Personas
* Process AI Agents
* System AI Agents
* Agent responsibilities
* Inputs
* Outputs
* Functionalities / requirements
* Other relevant relationships or dependencies

Your task is to analyze both:

1. The provided Excel workbook — this represents the target business/persona architecture.
2. The existing Underwriting solution codebase — this represents the agents and implementation that already exist.

The goal is to determine how the existing implementation can be aligned with the new persona-based architecture without unnecessarily rebuilding agents that already exist.

