PART 5 — Identify Overlapping Existing Agents

This is one of the most important parts.

Compare the agents/capabilities in the existing codebase against:

* Process AI Agents from the Excel
* System AI Agents from the Excel

Identify overlaps/reusable implementations.

The match does NOT need to be 100% identical.

A match should be considered if the existing implementation performs a substantially similar business or technical capability, even if:

* The name is different
* The implementation is structured differently
* The inputs are slightly different
* The outputs are slightly different
* The functionality is broader/narrower
* The existing agent performs additional responsibilities
* The Excel agent represents a refined version of the existing capability

Use functional similarity, not just name similarity.

For every potential overlap, classify it as:

Exact / Strong Match

Existing implementation essentially provides the required capability.

Partial Match

Existing implementation provides a significant portion of the required capability but needs modification.

Related / Weak Match

There is useful existing functionality, but substantial changes would be required.

No Match

No meaningful existing implementation was found.

Do NOT force a match simply because the names sound similar.

